  Kodama mass deposited at the shell, m_1(R_s+) - m_1(R_s-) = 2.00010e-02
  ADM mass of the seated object (limit)                       = 0
  lim r^3 phi_out (not compactly supported: fails phase1 D2) = -1/250000
  at r = 1: E = 1.95943e-02 L,  i.e. 2.63854e+25 kg per metre of L (c^2/G, foliation.py)

  transverse, this family:  INT extra dtau <= -(omega^2/8pi)/tau_p
  radial, every U=0 passage: INT extra dtau  = -(W_1 - 1)/(2 pi R)

  F1 hypotheses: spherical symmetry (-e^{2Phi}dt^2 + e^{2Lambda}dr^2 + R^2 dOmega^2); G_ab = 8 pi T_ab (T defined from the metric; convention tied to certify); U = 0: the sphere's areal radius held fixed throughout the passage; W > 0 at the sphere throughout (untrapped); the passage runs from f = 0 (flat) to f = 1 (seated)
  F2 adds:       outgoing radial null k = u + n, u Eulerian, normalised -u.k = 1
  transverse adds: this family only: p_T depends on the lapse and Lambda chosen; f is C^1 and at rest at both ends (f_tau = 0)

